WEBVTT

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.030
<b><i>John C. Stennis</i> CVN-74</b>

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.900
<b>U.S. Navy Carrier Strike Group Three</b>

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.250
<b><i>Halsey</i> DDG-97</b>

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.970
The sonar isn't working, 
and neither is the MAD!

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.100
The methane content of 
the air is rising!

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.800
What... the hell?!

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:42.910
Captain, the <i>Halsey</i>!

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:43.880
What?!

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.270
Could that be...

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:12.000
It's... an Evolutionary Invasion Object?

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:17.410
If it proceeds on its current course, 
it will reach the Panama Canal in about 19 hours.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.670
The U.S. Navy is taking heavy losses.

00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:22.550
However, they say dispatching 
E-gene holders is unnecessary.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.810
I wonder what that means.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.630
S-Seriously? There's no way...

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:11.130
Abilities of distinguished individuals, 
numerous throughout history,

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.400
have been stored in special E-genes.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.400
<b>E-genes</b>

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.000
The E-gene holders, 
who inherit those genes,

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.780
<b>AU balls</b>

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:22.760
summon the abilities sleeping 
within them via AU balls,

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:25.980
and embody AU weapons.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:32.150
The E-gene holders belonging to the 
supranational organization Dogoo

00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:35.150
versus enemies from outer space 
known as Evolutionary Invasion Objects.

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:38.670
This is the chronicle of their 
fateful battle for humanity!

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.190
Gun No. 7: Musashi Wonder.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:21.600
That's the <i>Yamato</i>, all right.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.000
What is an Evolutionary Invasion Object 
doing possessing and resurrecting the <i>Yamato</i>?

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:28.590
Plus, the <i>Yamato</i> sank way 
closer to Japan, and...

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.810
So this is one of Japan's "otaku"?

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:33.070
Ah— Wait!

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:36.110
This isn't the <i>Yamato</i>— it's the <i>Musashi</i>!

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:39.980
It doesn't have enough anti-aircraft guns, 
and it doesn't have the shielding...

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:45.060
So, uh, it's different... and...

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:50.950
Sorry! I don't really know that much 
about old battleships...

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:47.300
<b>Second thoughts </b>

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.800
<b>Misunderstanding </b>

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.020
<b>Totally a military otaku </b>

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.800
Maybe it's the <i>Yamato</i>, after all?

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.020
Just shut it for a second, Squirt!

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.320
I'm sorry...

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:04.600
We believe this Evolutionary Invasion Object 
is going to pass through the Panama Canal

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.220
and advance into the Atlantic Ocean.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:13.010
The U.S. Armed Forces are saying they will 
stake their reputations on stopping it.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:14.310
What do you mean?

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:17.420
It's their worst nightmare:

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:22.290
a battleship of the former Imperial Navy 
attacking via the Panama Canal.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:23.460
Oh...

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:28.430
In World War II, Japan tried to destroy 
the Panama Canal, or something...

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.430
<b>I-400 class submarine </b>

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.430
<b>M6A Seiran</b>

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:33.470
But the <i>Musashi</i> is too big! 
It can't get through the Panama Canal.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:37.370
It was built to surpass the American 
ships that were using the canal.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:38.760
Unfortunately...

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:42.660
It is now eminently possible 
for a ship of <i>Yamato</i>'s class

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:44.820
<b>1997: Construction began on the third set of locks</b>

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.820
<b>Possible for transit
Length: 366 m
Draft: 49 m {TB: Note, this is actually incorrect. The most incorrect part is that 49 is actually the feet, according to wikipedia. Draft is apparently a technical term (that seems appropriate here).}</b>

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:44.840
to make the transit.

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:47.210
W-When the heck did that happen?

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:51.620
They haven't forgotten ordinary 
soldiers have no chance

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.820
against Evolutionary Invasion 
Objects, have they?

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:58.180
They just gave official notice that they have 
not ruled out a thermonuclear attack.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:05:59.940
A thermonuclear attack?!

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.280
No way...

00:06:02.850 --> 00:06:06.480
That "boat" is the battleship's wreckage

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:09.920
being held together by countless 
tiny Invasion Objects.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:15.350
They're probably not worried about Invasion Objects as long as they vaporize the <i>Musashi</i>.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.130
But that's horrible!

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:21.050
Yeah, who knows what effect that could have 
on the Evolutionary Invasion Objects!

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.810
Not that!

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:24.470
Poor <i>Musashi</i>!

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:31.240
Anyway, we can't allow them 
to use nuclear weapons.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.540
<i>We're</i> sinking that ship.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:38.240
We're going to sink the <i>Musashi</i>...

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:40.170
Contact from H.Q.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:44.060
"We'll be calling our target the 
'<i>Musashi Wonder.</i>'" Over.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.470
The <i>Musashi Wonder</i>...?

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:51.700
Time to prepare a splendid strategy that 
won't cause the U.S. forces to lose face.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.130
<b>MQ-4C Triton </b>

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.140
We're counting on you, Galiko.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.650
And you are more than 
welcome to, Mr. Vidocq!

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:03.350
Io, Europa, Ganymede, Callisto!

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.140
We're off!

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:21.650
The U.S. forces seem to have begun 
prepping their nuclear attack.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:24.150
The Second Platoon has arrived 
at the <i>Clayton Forrester</i>.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:27.610
Will the special task force please 
report to the briefing room.

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:31.590
Look what I found: eggs!

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.860
Urk, nasty.

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:37.400
Are you saying we gotta smash the eggs 
before taking out the <i>Musashi Wonder</i>?

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:42.780
Well if you destroy the ship first, 
the eggs will be scattered.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:47.240
I can stomp the eggs, 
but how will we sink the ship?

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.330
Look at this.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:56.780
The tiny Cluster-class objects making up the 
<i>Musashi Wonder</i> do more than attack.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:01.200
They're also dividing up the 
look-out duty and propulsion.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.230
Smarter than they look, huh?

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:07.200
No, really stupid.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:08.310
Huh?

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:12.940
I get it. These guys are like 
worker bees and army ants.

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:14.760
Exactly.

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:17.180
What? Huh?

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:19.620
Which means that, somewhere, 
there's a smart one—

00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:22.760
or rather, something 
like a queen bee.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:29.980
Lacking intelligence, these objects are like 
stem cells before they differentiate.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:32.250
There must be a core uniting them

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:36.170
to build and operate the <i>Musashi Wonder.</i>

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:40.370
If we can just destroy that, then 
the whole cluster will collapse.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:44.730
And the <i>Musashi Wonder</i> will turn 
back into a heap of scrap?

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:48.480
At that point, the U.S. forces 
won't have a reason to move in. 

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:51.090
So that core resurrected the <i>Musashi</i>.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.960
The remains of the mob will 
be isolated in the water, 

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.900
and we can request that one of the 
other platoons deal with them. 

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:53.810
But why?

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:57.100
So then what's this "core"?

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:58.740
Galiko.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:01.130
Yessir! It's this.

00:09:03.030 --> 00:09:07.280
This thing... built the <i>Musashi</i>?

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:15.020
Yeah, this is definitely the <i>Musashi</i>...

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.220
What are you doing?

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:21.110
She was all, "Show me the 
<i>Musashi </i>observation data!"

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:25.870
Any Evolutionary Invasion Object that can 
reconstruct the <i>Musashi</i> so perfectly is awesome!

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:28.140
Umm, "awesome"?

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:32.240
Plus, to aim for the Panama Canal, it's like, 
wow, really hung up on this, huh!

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:36.060
Since it's come to this, I'd kinda like to 
see the <i>Musashi</i> make it through!

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:37.740
...is... just what I thought...

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:42.970
But why do the Evolutionary Invasion Objects 
know so much about the <i>Musashi</i>?

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:45.580
It's almost like somebody taught them.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:47.350
Let's go, Squirt!

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:49.210
What? Really?

00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:52.610
We got the okay from the U.S. 
forces. Operation is go.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:54.490
The U.S. forces?

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.760
Which means... 
Does that mean...?!

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:05.470
<i>John C. Stennis</i>, CVN-74!

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:09.900
Ready... go!

00:10:10.810 --> 00:10:14.650
To get them to lend us a ship like this, 
that's Mr. Vidocq's power at work!

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:19.790
I heard he told them he'd sink 
the <i>Musashi Wonder</i> for sure.

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:25.090
But we're the ones who'll be fighting.

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:32.460
Anyhow, if we don't beat the <i>Musashi Wonder</i> 
before it gets to the Panama Canal... nukes!

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:35.740
Right, so there's no room for failure.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:41.420
That's... 332... .9 m for you...

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.380
Ginormous!

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:48.390
Are you okay?

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:53.660
I made up my mind.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.990
Huh? About what?

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:59.260
I'm gonna be the one to sink 
the <i>Musashi Wonder</i>!

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.750
The <i>Musashi Wonder</i> has entered 
the area of operations.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:09.830
Understood.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:13.530
Members of the Second Platoon, 
are your preparations complete?

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:18.780
This is the <i>Alex Logan</i> rush squad. 
We're good to go.

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:25.780
This is the <i>John C. Stennis</i> shooter squad.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:43.940
We're good to go!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:56.890
Target confirmed!

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:00.140
The <i>Musashi... Wonder!</i>

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.980
Here are the positions of eggs and core.

00:12:04.650 --> 00:12:08.200
We'll destroy the upper part of this 
structure and ram a pod inside.

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.250
Then the first thing will be
to exterminate the eggs.

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:16.640
After that, we'll beat up the core, 
rendering it incapable of supporting the ship.

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.320
Jack and Newton are the rush squad.

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:22.690
Nobunagun will shoot open the 
hole for them to rush.

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:25.010
Gandhi will back her up.

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:26.270
Wait a minute!

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:29.990
AU weapons only work on 
Evolutionary Invasion Objects!

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:33.760
I thought they barely had any effect on 
armored plates like the ones battleships have!

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:35.570
That's right.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:39.540
And the <i>Musashi Wonder</i> is plastered 
with Invasion Objects to boot,

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:41.880
so conventional weapons 
won't work, either.

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:44.110
Huh? So then what'll we do?

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:47.290
Well... so...

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:53.190
Interesting! I'll do it!

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.920
Nobunagun has opened fire.

00:12:57.140 --> 00:13:00.770
Okay. Galiko, counting on you 
to monitor the impact.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:01.940
Got it!

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:05.420
Double check the data link 
with the U.S. flotilla.

00:13:05.420 --> 00:13:06.490
Roger.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:15.510
Just what you'd expect of a control tower with 
a maximum armor thickness of 500 mm.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:22.240
The concentration of Invasion Objects 
at the target point is decreasing!

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:24.520
Keep shooting just like that!

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:39.530
Here they come!

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:05.210
The concentration of Invasion Objects 
just needs to drop a little further...

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:08.320
And that's 0%!

00:14:09.220 --> 00:14:10.700
Let the attack begin!

00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:44.370
We did it!

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.510
Sorry, <i>Musashi</i>.

00:14:50.650 --> 00:14:52.990
Next! Get in there!

00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:55.420
We're up.

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:11.680
And the rush is a success.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.280
I'll take you to the eggs.

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:24.550
This way.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.780
Vidocq, we found the eggs.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:33.360
Wow!

00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:36.110
Newton, just like we planned.

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:38.170
Don't order me around.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.730
Hey, Vidocq!

00:15:40.490 --> 00:15:44.180
I'm gonna rush, too. We don't need to 
attack from the outside anymore, right?

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:45.310
But...

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:48.340
I want to sink the <i>Musashi</i>!

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:52.970
Here I come!

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:08.830
Let me have a little fun, too.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:18.240
Hey, c'mon. Are you serious?

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:20.780
I owe you one.

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:23.170
Captain—!

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:25.810
If we back down now, 
we'll be a worldwide laughingstock!

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:29.620
Let's get as close as we can!

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:49.950
Nobunagun is in.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:51.810
I'll guide her to the core Object!

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:54.430
Thanks, Galiko.

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:56.170
And? How are the eggs?

00:16:57.740 --> 00:16:58.960
Zeroed.

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:00.790
All clear here, too.

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:05.560
Then please back up Nobunagun. 
She's headed for the core Object now.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:07.690
She just does what she wants.

00:17:07.690 --> 00:17:08.750
Jeez.

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:21.570
So this is the core Object...

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:26.500
These guys are...

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:31.580
...the ones who took the quietly 
slumbering<i> Musashi,</i> and...

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:36.100
This is Nobunagun. Core Object 
identified! I'm taking it out!

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:53.560
Could those be...? No way...

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:57.120
This... is what happened 
to the <i>Musashi</i>?

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:22.030
These are <i>Musashi'</i>s— 
no, her crew's... memories?

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:28.310
These... The memories of those 
people built the <i>Musashi</i>.

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:34.100
Even so, this isn't the 
place for you guys.

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:39.170
Cut it out, already! 
At this rate, you'll be nuked.

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:46.420
Don't... do that... to <i>Musashi</i>...

00:18:55.950 --> 00:18:57.070
What're you waiting for?!

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:00.260
Hurry up and take out 
the core Object!

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:00.870
R-Right!

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:04.360
Farewell...

00:19:04.360 --> 00:19:06.860
...<i>Musashi</i>!

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:46.520
The <i>Musashi Wonder</i> is sinking!

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.030
And the Second Platoon?

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:52.870
Everyone escaped without issue.

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:58.130
Good night.

00:19:59.580 --> 00:20:02.730
Rest in peace, <i>Musashi.</i>

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:22.280
The <i>Musashi Wonder</i> is at 
500 m and sinking.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:25.900
How deep is the oceanic trench 
in Central America?

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:30.340
Ah. It was 6,669 m, if I'm not mistaken.

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:35.890
It is possible for them to survive under 
that much water pressure?

00:20:36.320 --> 00:20:39.060
That's... hard to say...

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:42.550
But I don't think they'll be 
able to return so easily.

00:20:44.980 --> 00:20:49.670
The disappointment and frustration of the 
<i>Musashi</i> and her crew, sunk in 1944,

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:53.820
encountered the Evolutionary 
Invasion Objects in the deep.

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:56.960
Then, to achieve their earnest desire
 of invading the American mainland,

00:20:56.960 --> 00:21:02.580
they took years to have the <i>Musashi</i> revived.

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:05.220
That's what you're saying?

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:07.350
Sounds pretty occult to me.

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:11.850
It's not "occult"! I actually saw it!

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:16.420
Uh... Uh, Galileo?

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.970
Oh, man...

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:21.090
That is one boring swimsuit.

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:19.920
<b>Ogura</b>

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:21.170
<b>School-designated 
swimwear </b>

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:26.160
Th-This is all my m-mom 
packed for me!

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:29.710
Oh! One of those Japanese 
school swimsuits!

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:33.020
Get back here!

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:34.320
School swimsuit!

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:35.880
Give it back!

00:21:34.880 --> 00:21:36.750
School swimsuit! 

00:21:38.580 --> 00:21:40.060
They get along so well.

00:21:40.310 --> 00:21:44.480
<b>The Second Platoon:
On leave </b>

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:54.910
<b>The First Platoon:
Reporting for duty </b>

00:23:25.420 --> 00:23:27.810
Today we decide who'll be the new gopher!

00:23:27.990 --> 00:23:29.080
Huh? Why me, too?

00:23:29.080 --> 00:23:30.640
Let's make it a fair fight!

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:33.510
Quit yer gripin' and all three of 
you go buy some bread!

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:35.040
Yessirrrrr!

